  - systemd-zram-generator (installed version: 1.2.1-2+b2)

# FIXME: I have not yet confirmed this is safe!! --twb, January 2026
#
# Recently (January 2026) the Debian Security Team started warning about libsoup.
# https://salsa.debian.org/debian/debian-security-support/-/commit/8ed15071d7716260b1c0666c59bab1dd8166c3c6
# https://bugs.debian.org/1109118
# https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libsoup/-/commit/2a9d8ecc45bb814f6a81b1241e6c0c55d632aa28
#
# I confirm that libsoup is already in desktop-inmate-amc-latest at AMC.
# i.e. this is not a newly-INTRODUCED risk, this is a newly-DISCLAIMED risk.
#
#     root@amc:~# grep -l ^Package:.libsoup  /srv/netboot/images/*latest/dpkg.status
#     /srv/netboot/images/desktop-inmate-amc-latest/dpkg.status
#     /srv/netboot/images/desktop-inmate-amc-library-latest/dpkg.status
#     /srv/netboot/images/desktop-staff-amc-latest/dpkg.status
#
# What we SHOULD do is:
# * look at what packages we use pull in libsoup
# * replace them if reasonable to do so
# * then denylist libsoup in prisonpc-ersatz (and build a new version of that)
# * OTHERWISE, accept the risk in grepF because what else can we do?
#
# In --template=desktop,
#
#     xfce4-screenshooter : Depends: libsoup-3.0-0 (>= 3.0.3) but it is not going to be installed
#
# In --template=desktop-staff,
#
#     gvfs-backends : Depends: libsoup-3.0-0 (>= 3.0.3) but it is not going to be installed
#     xfce4-screenshooter : Depends: libsoup-3.0-0 (>= 3.0.3) but it is not going to be installed
#
# In --template=desktop-inmate there is no problem.
#
#     2. gnucash:amd64=1:5.6-1~bpo12+1 Depends libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 (>= 2.34.6~)
#     libwebkit2gtk-4.1-0 : Depends: libsoup-3.0-0 (>= 3.0.3) but it is not going to be installed
#
# Replacing the screenshot app seemed easy.
# Rebuilding the gvfs backends for staff so it includes only the SFTP driver (and not e.g. the GDrive driver) at COMPILE TIME is a bit harder.
# We can tell AMC 'sorry gnucash is not in the app list anymore due to minor security risks'.
#
# AFAICT AMC have never actually run gnucash at all, so they should not miss it.
# https://github.com/cyberitsolutions/bootstrap2020/blob/main/doc/popcon/popcon_2025-01-01_to_2025-06-30.csv
# [and other 6monthly reports]
#
# The *actual* risk here is if you use libsoup as a server, and
# PROBABLY none of the packages we currently/will use,
# will use libsoup as a SERVER.
# But we cannot tell at package build time whether a package is using the server parts of libsoup!
* Source:libsoup3
  Details: Only supported as a client, not as a server: see https://gitlab.gnome.org/GNOME/libsoup/-/commit/2a9d8ecc45bb814f6a81b1241e6c0c55d632aa28
  Affected binary packages:
  - libsoup-3.0-0:amd64 (installed version: 3.6.6-1)
  - libsoup-3.0-common (installed version: 3.6.6-1)
